<p>BTS returned to the stage in Seoul on March 21 with a free comeback concert, their first performance as a full group in nearly four years. The show drew huge crowds in the South Korean capital and streamed globally on Netflix. Attendance figures varied: local estimates put the crowd at around 40,000 across central Seoul, while the group’s label said more than 100,000 fans took part in or around the event. The concert took place at Gwanghwamun Square in central Seoul. The comeback came a day after the release of BTS’s new album, &quot;ARIRANG&quot;. The label said the album sold nearly 4 million copies on its first day.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TA1IIeI0Grh-U02Eoai3NTrG2d8Snqo3V4jHSvhBDF9PhR4kwhQ8deDOr0iIvzm0IgnZEbnAmY38o4HUDb_Ao14dNKo1zG5yIsw4ID9RR689gRVV_CpNCkH8sZQ1Pd3uGt-pISLxVHbu_17x2AGfr84tTay6V0CK5u5DeLP02zQu1zQoY61pIp6UCyvenUe0KpLiWZfteDt-HTyvEMSyKxuwzhoctbgIp2QhFDrFc_4_NTYg9vsLuKzbUw4ErmO4sgk6ZFWbN0UB_xj5fA' alt='South Korean megastars BTS reunited for their first show in nearly four years.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Setlist focus: The New York Times said the performance leaned heavily on songs from &quot;ARIRANG&quot; rather than mostly older hits.</li><li>Album identity: The Hindu said &quot;ARIRANG&quot; was presented as reflecting the band’s maturing Korean identity.</li><li>Performance strain: RM performed through an ankle injury during the concert, according to The New York Times.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>BTS label: The group’s label said the Seoul comeback drew more than 100,000 fans and that &quot;ARIRANG&quot; sold nearly 4 million copies on its first day. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/music/bts-draws-over-100000-fans-to-seoul-comeback-concert-label/article70771418.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Analysts: Analysts quoted in reporting said the Seoul launch could mark the start of the biggest K-pop tour yet in both scale and revenue. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/article-bts-arirang-k-pop-tour-launch-netflix-seoul-concert/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The Times described the concert as a homecoming in Seoul’s historic center and a reminder of BTS’s role in South Korean soft power. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/21/world/bts-netflix-concert-arirang'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/k-pop-sensation-bts-returns-with-a-free-comeback-concert-in-seoul-after-a-4-year-hiatus'>K-pop sensation BTS returns with a free comeback concert in Seoul after a 4-year hiatus</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/k-pop-giants-bts-celebrate-return-with-seoul-concert/a-76469022'>K-pop giants BTS celebrate return with Seoul concert</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/article-bts-arirang-k-pop-tour-launch-netflix-seoul-concert/'>K-pop supergroup BTS returns in Seoul concert after four-year hiatus</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/21/world/bts-netflix-concert-arirang'>BTS’s Comeback Show Was Heavy on Their New Album</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/entertainment/music/bts-draws-over-100000-fans-to-seoul-comeback-concert-label/article70771418.ece'>BTS draws over 100,000 fans to Seoul comeback concert: label</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/bts-comeback-reunion-concert-seoul-korea-netflix/'>BTS kicks off global tour with South Korea concert</a> - cbsnews.com</li></ul>